---
code: cli-flag-value-not-a-number
when-fires: a numeric flag was given a non-number. cli/lib.rs parse_expect_count (--expect-files). {flag} and the {got} token.
why: 27R section 8b: --expect-files is a CI scope assertion, so a malformed count is refused rather than coerced - a silently-zero expectation would pass vacuously.
edit-loop: edit a sentence in the transcript below, then run `mise run loom:compile -- cli-flag-value-not-a-number && mise run loom:promote -- cli-flag-value-not-a-number`. `mise run loom:vars -- --all cli-flag-value-not-a-number` lists this case's values; type {{name}} to insert or move one.
---
-- replay --
$ dorc lint --expect-files=many oracle.sh
error[cli-flag-value-not-a-number]: sm --expect-files needs a non-negative
integer, got `many`
